      "inversion": "J is reflection x->-x in logarithmic coordinates; Fourier residue classes are not substituted for inversion parity",
      "physical_interval": "I_lambda=[-log(lambda),log(lambda)]=[-L/2,L/2] with L=2*log(lambda) and Lebesgue measure in logarithmic coordinates",
      "pole_signs": "the inversion-even pole is +2|cosh(x/2)><cosh(x/2)| and the inversion-odd pole is -2|sinh(x/2)><sinh(x/2)|",
      "prime_endpoint": "every prime power n<=lambda^2 is retained at the inclusive endpoint, and lambda is never confused with lambda^2",
      "prime_sign": "m_lambda=2*theta_prime-2*sum_(n<=lambda^2) Lambda(n)/sqrt(n)*cos(t*log(n))",
      "runtime_version": "the interval runtime must report mpmath==1.4.1 exactly; a mismatch is rejected before any interval probe",
      "source_interval": "[-lambda,lambda] with Lebesgue measure and zero extension; the source normalization, zero-Lebesgue-integral correction, and actual source Gram C^*C are retained",
